2026-10-23T10:14:28.4694980Z    [0m[36m┌─[0m /home/runner/work/rust-agentic-foundations/rust-agentic-foundations/Cargo.lock:26:1
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4696242Z    [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4697372Z [0m[36m26[0m [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31mctutils 0.4.3 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index[0m
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4699603Z    [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[0m [0m[31msecurity vulnerability detected[0m
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4701796Z    [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4702359Z    [0m[36m├[0m ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0385
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4703338Z    [0m[36m├[0m Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0385
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4704231Z    [0m[36m├[0m ## Summary
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4704705Z      
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4711466Z      The `ctutils::Choice` type has mask generation functions for each unsigned
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4712133Z      integer size (`u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `u128`). These are `const fn` and
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4712750Z      therefore can't reuse the `asm!`-backed mask generation in the `cmov` crate
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4713315Z      that's otherwise used to ensure constant-time.
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4713683Z      
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4714057Z      In releases prior to v0.4.4, the generated code from these functions could
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4714690Z      include a branch on commonly used platforms. This has been corrected in this
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4715283Z      release and now verified on several platforms using BINSEC.
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4715686Z      
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4716101Z      Additionally, `u128` comparison operations provided via `ctutils::Choice` and
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4716769Z      intended to work in constant-time were generating branches on 32-bit targets.
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4717412Z      This has been resolved via a special case implementation of these functions
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4717914Z      for such targets.
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4718472Z      
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4718682Z      ## Impact
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4718917Z      
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4719282Z      Branch instructions on secret values can potentially leak such values via
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4719935Z      covert channels. This can enable attackers to potentially recover such secrets.
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4720414Z      
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4720610Z      ## Resolution
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4720850Z      
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4721245Z      This has been resolved by calling `Choice::to_u8()` when generating the mask,
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4721854Z      which in turn uses `black_box` as an optimization barrier. Verification that
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4722477Z      this resulted in the desired change in the generated assembly across a variety
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4723080Z      of target CPU architectures was performed by BINSEC, which now runs
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4723571Z      automatically in CI using `cargo checkct`.
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4724260Z    [0m[36m├[0m Announcement: https://github.com/RustCrypto/utils/pull/1569
2026-10-23T10:14:28.4725005Z    [0m[36m├[0m Solution: Upgrade to >=0.4.4 (try `cargo update -p ctutils`)
